  <!-- 3. 24-48H DELTA -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>The US Treasury Office of Foreign Assets Control confirmed that the special-purpose authorization for Iranian crude oil transactions expired at midnight on 2026-08-21, with no renewal notice published on treasury.gov/ofac as of 07:00 UTC on the same date. No mediator channel — Oman, Qatar, or Switzerland — published a readout in the 72-hour window surrounding the expiration, and the White House had not announced a revised schedule for US-Iran contacts as of press time. → moved <span class="cite">F1</span>, <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>Lloyd's List Intelligence published its Strait of Hormuz Brief on 2026-08-19, recording 73 commercial transits over the preceding seven days, an average of approximately 10.4 vessels per day against a pre-war baseline of approximately 94 per day. The Brief noted that dark contacts — vessels transmitting no AIS signal — exceeded AIS-visible transits for the first time since the strait's closure, attributed by the analysis to alternative-operator routing. Operation Project Freedom mine-countermeasure activities continued with no cleared-corridor announcement as of the publication date. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>US President Trump posted on Truth Social on 2026-08-10 demanding that Iran pay compensation for US asset damage before Washington would consider extending the sanctions authorization; Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Baghaei rejected this publicly on 2026-08-11 as a unilateral precondition outside any agreed framework. These statements established the public opening positions of both governments as the MOU expired six days later on 2026-08-17 (Al Jazeera confirmed). → moved <span class="cite">F1</span>, supports <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>Haaretz reported on 2026-08-18, citing unnamed Israeli security officials, that Iranian and Israeli forces had not conducted direct exchanges since a halt-strikes compact reached on 2026-06-28 — confirmed by Axios as a US-brokered agreement on the same date. The officials described the current posture as a 'managed freeze' but noted that the compact was informal and its post-MOU-expiration status formally undefined. IRGC-linked and Hezbollah forces remained at high readiness in southern Lebanon and western Syria as of 2026-08-18 per the same officials. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>Channel 12 polling data published 2026-08-18 and reported by Haaretz placed a bloc led by Benny Gantz and Gadi Eisenkot at 61 seats in simulated ballots — one seat short of a majority — with the 2026-10-27 election date confirmed as the statutory endpoint. Netanyahu governed in caretaker capacity following the coalition's formal loss of parliamentary majority in July 2026. The caretaker government holds reduced legislative authority and has not submitted new military-authorization requests as of this date. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

