      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (38%):</strong> Derived primarily from F4 (IRGC/Hezbollah strike probability 38% through Sept 15): the halt-strikes compact's post-MOU status is undefined, IRGC forces are at high readiness, and sanctions re-imposition today removes an economic brake on Iranian proxy activity.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (45%):</strong> Base case: the informal compact holds into October despite MOU expiration, Hormuz remains near 10 transits per day (F3 NO, p=0.88), and neither side forces a resolution before Israel's Oct 27 election imposes a freeze on both Netanyahu's caretaker government and US interlocutors.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (17%):</strong> A chained probability: F2 YES (session by Sept 4, p=0.25) AND F5 YES (enrichment cap by Oct 15, p=0.18) AND F1 YES (sanctions extension, p=0.18) — any one link failing collapses the path; the dark-fleet phenomenon (Lloyd's List, 2026-08-19) provides a partial economic pressure release that could reduce both sides' urgency to negotiate rapidly.</p>
    </div>
